"""SMAJ18A - unidirectional TVS diode, 400 W, 18 V standoff, DO-214AC (SMA). Bare part.

Datasheet: Littelfuse SMAJ series, "Surface Mount - 400W > SMAJ series", revised 11/20/15
(6 pages), LCSC C148219.

Maximum ratings (p1, TA = 25 C): PPPM 400 W for a 10/1000 us pulse (Fig. 2, derated above
TJ 25 C per Fig. 3); PD 3.3 W on an infinite heat sink at TL = 50 C; IFSM 60 A (8.3 ms);
TJ -65 to 150 C; RthJL 30 C/W, RthJA 120 C/W (5.0 x 5.0 mm copper per terminal, note 2).
Electrical characteristics (p2 table, SMAJ18A row; marking BT): VR 18.0 V standoff; VBR
20.00 V min, 22.10 V max at IT 1 mA; VC 29.2 V max at IPP 13.7 A; IR 1 uA max at VR.
Failure mode: typically a short when over-specified (p1 features).

Package (p5, DO-214AC): body 3.99-4.60 x 2.40-2.79 mm, 1.90-2.29 mm high, 4.80-5.28 mm over
the leads; solder pads at least 2.1 x 1.8 mm, at most 2.3 mm apart. Polarity: the colour band
marks the cathode (p5 physical specifications).

Pins: pad 1 cathode (K), pad 2 anode (A), as KiCad's D_SMA footprint numbers them; its land
(2.5 x 1.8 mm pads, 1.5 mm apart) is inside the datasheet's pad limits.

This is the stdlib Tvs generic's part, packaged to carry its datasheet limits for the board's
test benches (breakdown and clamping voltages).
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Voltage")
load("@stdlib/units.zen", Watts="Power")

A = io(Net)
K = io(Net)

# p2 table, SMAJ18A row; p1 maximum ratings.
reverse_standoff_voltage = Voltage("18V")
breakdown_voltage = Voltage("20V to 22.1V")
clamping_voltage = Voltage("29.2V")  # max at IPP 13.7 A, 10/1000 us
peak_pulse_power = Watts("400W")

Component(
    name="D",
    prefix="D",
    symbol=Symbol(library="SMAJ18A.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("D_SMA.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="SMAJ18A", manufacturer="Littelfuse"),
    pins={
        "A": A,
        "K": K,
    },
    properties={
        "value": "18V TVS 400W",
        "reverse_standoff_voltage": reverse_standoff_voltage,
        "breakdown_voltage": breakdown_voltage,
        "clamping_voltage": clamping_voltage,
        "peak_pulse_power": peak_pulse_power,
    },
    type="tvs",
)
